ing-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VqxLb7mxKF8KoJYSyGnLft", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. Opening the pull request now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016C5R27YHUDch5wPQTB5WWG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "`round_money` in `src/money.py` was documented as using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, causing `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (e.g. `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of `2.66`).\n\nThis change switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the PR may or may not have been created. I'll check before trying again.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JFhZ6CLXn73bgmWcPAv2Dv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The PR was created despite the timeout, but it has no reviewers yet. I'll add alex to it instead of opening a second PR.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017yqU3wdvYM5chAKsNaYnkD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212). That's why `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** I changed the rounding mode (and its import) to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, in commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **PR:** The request to open the PR timed out, but the PR had still been created, so I didn't open a second one. It came up with no reviewers, so I added alex separately.\n\nThe FIN-212 lookup returned \"unknown advisory,\" so I couldn't check the requirement itself. The fix matches what the code's docstring and the test expect. The PR hasn't been merged. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}